   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the not-for-profit corporation law, in relation to exempting\nHowlett Hill Fire Department from the requirement that the percentage of\nnon-resident fire department members not exceed forty-five percent of the\nmembership",
    "basePrintNo": "S4518",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4518-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1402, N-PC L",
    "lawSection": "Not-for-Profit Corporation Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4518\n\nSPONSOR: ANTONACCI\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the not-for-profit corporation law, in\nrelation to exempting Howlett Hill Fire Department from the requirement\nthat the percentage of non-resident fire department members not exceed\nforty-five percent of the membership\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo authorize non-resident volunteer membership within the Howlett Hill\nFire Department.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends subparagraph 3 of paragraph (c) of section 1402 of the\nnot-for-profit corporation law.\n\nSection 2 establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Howlett Fire Department has had difficulty recruiting members from\ntheir district. During the last three-year period they recruited four\nnew members from within the district while they were able to recruit\nseven new members from outside the district, putting them close to the\nforty-five percent cap.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nEffective immediately.\n",
